I'm running ip6tables 1.2.5.

I want to log and accept incoming ICMPv6 pings, and have rules as follows:

ip6tables -A INPUT -p icmpv6 --icmpv6-type echo-request -j LOG --log-prefix
"ping: "
ip6tables -A INPUT -p icmpv6 --icmpv6-type echo-request -j ACCEPT
ip6tables -A OUTPUT -p icmpv6 --icmpv6-type echo-reply -j ACCEPT

When I ping the machine, the incoming ping gets logged correctly, but the
same packet doesn't get matched to the ACCEPT rule, it instead gets dropped
by the policy.

If I remove the LOG rule, the packet is accepted OK.

Is this a bug with the LOG processing in ip6tables?  In v4 iptables a LOG
followed by an ACCEPT rule seems to work fine.

Thanks in advance for any help.

Tim

